# Design System

- Search for and reuse an existing component before adding one. Extend shared
  primitives instead of duplicating implementations.
- Use design tokens for color, spacing, typography, radii, shadows, and motion.
  Do not add random one-off styling or arbitrary values without a documented need.
- Prefer shadcn/ui and Radix primitives where appropriate; use Lucide icons.
- Keep the visual language polished and age-neutral. Avoid generic Bootstrap
  styling, excessive gradients, rounded-card grids, glassmorphism, and cartoons.
- Use Motion for React sparingly and honor reduced-motion preferences.
- Make responsive behavior intentional from 375px through large desktops.
